{"id": "EUVD-2026-92813", "enisaUuid": "c44fcbd9-b12a-32f7-9a2e-8d4538ff0ec2", "description": "Insufficient boundary validation in the USB boot mode implementation of AMD Zynq\u2122 UltraScale+ MPSoC and RFSoC devices could allow unbounded Device Firmware Upgrade (DFU) download requests to overflow the DDR receive buffer into FSBL memory, potentially resulting in unauthorized code execution during the boot process. This issue could impact the confidentiality, integrity, or availability of affected system.", "datePublished": "2026-10-05T21:38:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T13:49:03", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.amd.com/en/resources/product-security/bulletin/AMD-SB-8029.html"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-0461", "GHSA-2xg6-gqcc-77jw"], "assigner": "AMD", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "198ce251-fba6-39d0-8bb5-4f842f5adc88", "product": {"name": "Zynq\u2122 UltraScale+ MPSoCs", "vendor": {"name": "AMD"}}, "product_version": "patch: 2026.1"}, {"id": "2773ed02-51a2-3d12-b97e-cb487e219e15", "product": {"name": "Kria SOMs", "vendor": {"name": "AMD"}}, "product_version": "patch: 2026.1"}, {"id": "51d9a8d5-86cd-3e82-b916-65c8793548f7", "product": {"name": "Zynq\u2122 UltraScale+ RFSoCs", "vendor": {"name": "AMD"}}, "product_version": "patch: 2026.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "49829ec0-25cc-34ae-acac-8422fa2eb277", "vendor": {"name": "AMD"}}], "isExploited": false}